1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,240
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,690
Grandma, what's wrong?
Does your stomach hurt?

4
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,560
No, Su Ah. I'm okay.

5
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:23,090
Why is it acting up
all of a sudden again?

6
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:24,900
Grandma.

7
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:38,540
Da Mi.

8
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:46,180
Grandma.

9
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:55,090
Sweetie, Su Ah. Grandma is fine.

10
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:57,600
Do not cry, okay?

11
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,330
They said you have to go to the
hospital when you have a boo-boo.

12
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,640
Go to the hospital
and get a shot, Grandma.

13
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,710
Yes, all right.

14
00:01:08,710 --> 00:01:10,210
Grandma will go to the hospital.

15
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:11,980
Do not cry, sweetheart.

16
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:25,590
(Episode 40)

17
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:27,360
You can head over
to the reception desk.

18
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,360
Thanks.

19
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,530
- Here.
- Thank you.

20
00:01:35,130 --> 00:01:36,270
Ms. Jo Mi Mi?

21
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:38,370
Yes, you are all done
with your checkup.

22
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:41,540
The results will be sent
via text message within two weeks.

23
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:43,880
- Yes, thank you.
- You are welcome.

24
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:00,860
(Calls)

25
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,530
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

26
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:03,860
She must be busy.

27
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:07,970
Is she sick or something, too?

28
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,500
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

29
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,850
Why do I look like this?

30
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,560
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

31
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:41,730
(Switching to Multimedia Message...)

32
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:49,540
Hey sweetie, I finished my checkup.

33
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,110
I did everything you told me to,
so praise me.

34
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,350
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

35
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,750
(I did everything you told me to,
so praise me.)

36
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:02,750
She must really have her hands full.

37
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,860
I need to get back
before the dinner rush.

38
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:16,940
Here you go.

39
00:03:20,370 --> 00:03:21,540
These are the originals.

40
00:03:26,950 --> 00:03:27,950
Thank you.

41
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:49,100
She's finally done it.
Good job, Ms. Mi Mi.

42
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:59,740
Well done. Good job, Madam Mi Mi.

43
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,720
You called yesterday.
I missed it, sorry.

44
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:09,050
Are you okay, Mom?

45
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,790
Let me know as soon as
the results come out. Promise.

46
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:17,060
Kang Da Mi.

47
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,960
Yes?

48
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:20,770
Could you come over here
for a moment?

49
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:22,270
Yes, on my way.

50
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,710
- What is it?
- You need to be able to tell...

51
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:32,880
every single color here apart,

52
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,680
so memorize all
the sample numbers, too.

53
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:37,950
By when?

54
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:41,390
An hour should be plenty, right?

55
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,290
An hour? Not even a whole day?

56
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:47,490
Three hours, then. Happy?

57
00:04:48,030 --> 00:04:49,660
Yes, thank you.

58
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,740
What was the number
for cobalt blue again?

59
00:04:58,370 --> 00:04:59,370
Was it 15?

60
00:05:00,410 --> 00:05:03,740
Was it 51? Seriously...

61
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,180
Da Mi?

62
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:08,710
Hello, Team Leader Cha.

63
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,150
What are you memorizing
so frantically?

64
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:13,350
What did the head designer
give you this time?

65
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:16,720
I have to memorize
fabric swatch numbers,

66
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:20,390
but I do not have much time,
so I am getting a bit frantic.

67
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,830
You can memorize them faster
by reversing it.

68
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:27,500
- Pardon?
- Instead of memorizing the names first,

69
00:05:27,970 --> 00:05:29,470
go with what number one is,
what number two is,

70
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,800
in that order.

71
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,040
If you group similar shades...

72
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:37,540
and map out their numbers first,
it is much easier to memorize.

73
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:42,080
Thank you, Assistant Manager Kang.

74
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:45,550
I will get going now.

75
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:57,230
Why are you looking at me like that?

76
00:05:57,730 --> 00:06:00,830
It is just nice to see you
helping out the assistant.

77
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:04,670
Helping is what
a senior colleague should do.

78
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,740
Still, it feels good to be praised.

79
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:18,680
I am so glad
I got this from Gangwon Province...

80
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:20,380
and stocked up early.

81
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:23,690
Is Seung Yun running late?

82
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,420
Mother, we are home.

83
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:28,760
Mother, you know,
she was so worried about you,

84
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:31,530
and right after work,
she came straight over...

85
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,460
Wait, what is all this honey for?

86
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,830
None of it is yours,
so mind your own business.

87
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:40,140
Are you going to have it
all to yourself?

88
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,510
At least let us have a taste.

89
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,680
Do not covet
what belongs to Seung Yun.

90
00:06:48,410 --> 00:06:50,450
All right, fine.

91
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:58,690
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

92
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,500
Oh, no.

93
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,670
What is wrong?
Is your stomach acting up again?

94
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:14,110
It is nothing, so hurry up
and prep for opening.

95
00:07:15,210 --> 00:07:17,640
Okay, got it.

96
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,020
Hello?

97
00:07:29,590 --> 00:07:31,620
Is this Ms. Jo Mi Mi's mobile phone?

98
00:07:31,890 --> 00:07:34,230
This is Haedeul University Hospital
Checkup Center.

99
00:07:34,690 --> 00:07:35,890
Yes, this is her.

100
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,330
While reviewing
your checkup results,

101
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,000
we found something
that requires further examination,

102
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,300
which is why we are calling.

103
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:43,500
If possible, we would like you
to visit today...

104
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,000
to discuss the findings.

105
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,800
Today?

106
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:50,510
You told me the results
would take about two weeks...

107
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,080
Besides, I run a business,

108
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:56,050
so it is difficult for me
to come in right away.

109
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:59,380
There is something
we need to check first.

110
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,620
You really should come in
as soon as possible.

111
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:03,320
Are you unavailable today?

112
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:08,890
I do not think I can make it today.
Could I come tomorrow instead?

113
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:11,960
Okay.

114
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:14,770
I will come in as soon as possible.

115
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:21,710
Mom.

116
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:23,740
Make me some food.

117
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:28,380
Fix it yourself.
Can you not see I am busy?

118
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,520
Where is Grandma?

119
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:35,120
I think she is still
lying down in bed.

120
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:50,700
Mother, I'm coming in.

121
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:59,040
Mother.

122
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:01,550
Please have at least a bite.

123
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,080
I reheated the radish soup.

124
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,220
I will not eat.

125
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:11,560
You skipped breakfast, too.
You will upset your stomach.

126
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:15,390
It turned rotten inside
a long time ago.

127
00:09:16,130 --> 00:09:18,760
Eating is not going to fix it.

128
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,100
Hitting Hak Sung...

129
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:28,340
was wrong of me to do
in front of you.

130
00:09:30,310 --> 00:09:31,580
I am sorry for that.

131
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,480
So please eat something.

132
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:37,180
I have lived too long.

133
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,820
I have lived for so long,

134
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:42,720
so I have seen it all,

135
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:45,390
the good and the bad.

136
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:17,150
Dae Chi.

137
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:21,030
Kang Dae Chi, come down here.

138
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,500
He said he was working from home.

139
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:28,430
Where did he go?

140
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,640
I told you I would be
unreachable for a while.

141
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:37,680
Why do you keep following me?

142
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,440
Did you not hear me?
Do you need me to repeat it?

143
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,210
How on earth are you
going to track down Kim Pro,

144
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,480
Kim Dong Seok, or whoever...

145
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:47,790
I mean, how are you going to capture
the guy who scammed you, Mr. Kang?

146
00:10:47,950 --> 00:10:50,420
I will track him down,
whatever it takes.

147
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,560
I will find that guy,

148
00:10:52,590 --> 00:10:56,030
clear my name of embezzlement,
and properly restore my honor first.

149
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,160
Go.

150
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,460
I'm sure I'm not your only debtor.

151
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,500
Are you just telling me that...

152
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:05,540
while planning to flee the country?

153
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:10,780
Look here, Ms. Cha Se Na. As for me,

154
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,910
I have lived my whole life
on nothing but pride, all right?

155
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:16,950
Grandma always said pride
does not put food on the table.

156
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:21,550
Pride has kept me fed all this time,
and from here on out,

157
00:11:21,590 --> 00:11:22,820
it will keep putting food
on my table.

158
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,060
Just go.

159
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,120
Once I catch that bastard,
you will be the first to know.

160
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:34,930
Wait. When it comes to tracking down
people who took off with money,

161
00:11:35,530 --> 00:11:37,640
Grandma is the absolute best
in this country.

162
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,750
It was hectic with so many patients,
wasn't it?

163
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:51,350
Lunchtime is long past.
How about some chicken soup?

164
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,380
Chicken soup?

165
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:57,420
- Do you mean across the street?
- Yes, Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.

166
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:00,320
The owner is a wonderful cook.

167
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:05,460
That is all right.
You should go ahead without me.

168
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,570
I really do not have
an appetite right now.

169
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:09,570
You should eat something.

170
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:12,300
Once afternoon clinic starts,
you will not have time again.

171
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:13,670
Let's go.

172
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:15,510
No, I...

173
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:18,340
I have a few things
to clean up here.

174
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,850
You can do that after we return.

175
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:31,290
Okay.

176
00:12:32,390 --> 00:12:34,960
I would rather jump into hellfire.

177
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:45,070
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

178
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,700
Hello, ma'am.

179
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,540
Hello, Director Ju,
have you not eaten...

180
00:12:54,610 --> 00:12:56,110
This is one of our staff.

181
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:58,620
- Park Ji Young.
- Yes.

182
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:00,620
Hello.

183
00:13:01,890 --> 00:13:03,450
Hello. Come on in.

184
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,160
Where should we sit?

185
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:09,230
- Please, have a seat right here.
- Thank you.

186
00:13:09,590 --> 00:13:10,590
Over here.

187
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,940
Two chicken soups, please.

188
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:21,940
Okay.

189
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:29,950
What do we do, Mi Mi?

190
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:37,390
Excuse me.

191
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,490
I don't see Mrs. Choi today.

192
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:46,030
- Where did she go?
- She is at home.

193
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:48,500
She hasn't been feeling well today.

194
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:49,670
Is she sick?

195
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:52,400
I noticed she was not
around earlier.

196
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:57,540
Well, she said she has no appetite,
so she hasn't eaten anything.

197
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:58,940
She has been in bed all day.

198
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,820
Is Mrs. Choi not feeling well?

199
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,480
No, it is nothing.

200
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:09,690
She just hasn't had much of an appetite.

201
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,160
Bring her to the clinic
if she still cannot eat.

202
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,420
I will examine her.

203
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,660
All right, thank you.

204
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:29,370
It is hot. Be careful, Ji Young.

205
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:32,840
- Yes, Director Ju.
- Yes.

206
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:36,680
Mother hasn't eaten anything?

207
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,890
What is going on?

208
00:14:42,050 --> 00:14:43,890
Honey, what does Mother like to eat?

209
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,320
Mom?
Why are you asking all of a sudden?

210
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:48,190
You know what she likes.

211
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:51,160
- What does she enjoy eating?
- I mean,

212
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:54,300
why are you asking
about what my mom likes?

213
00:14:54,570 --> 00:14:57,640
Why is it so strange
for me to care for my mother-in-law?

214
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:00,700
Of course it is strange.
You used to cringe...

215
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:02,140
every time someone
even brought her up.

216
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:05,210
Fine, lecture me later.

217
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,180
Just tell me,
I don't have much time.

218
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:08,780
Fish-shaped red bean pastries.

219
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,880
What? Fish-shaped pastries?

220
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:13,220
The stall at the entrance
of our neighborhood alley.

221
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,890
The fish-shaped pastries
filled with red bean.

222
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:17,050
She loves those.

223
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:18,990
Is that all? Anything else?

224
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:21,630
When I bought them for her before,

225
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:23,790
she would eat two or three
in one sitting.

226
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,800
She said they tasted even better...

227
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:28,630
because her son bought them.

228
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:32,800
Got it. The fish-shaped pastries
filled with red bean.

229
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:35,040
- I'm hanging up.
- Where are you right now?

230
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:48,490
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

231
00:15:48,650 --> 00:15:50,650
(Fish-Shaped Pastries)

232
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,460
Hello?

233
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:58,500
Mother, it's me, Ji Young.

234
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:02,000
Ji Young? Who is that?

235
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:06,900
Your daughter-in-law.
I called to see how you are doing.

236
00:16:07,370 --> 00:16:08,870
Is anyone home?

237
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:10,870
How can you call yourself
my daughter-in-law?

238
00:16:11,410 --> 00:16:13,710
What nonsense
are you calling to spew?

239
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:19,680
I have something to give you.
I'm outside your house right now.

240
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,450
You are outside where?

241
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:22,920
No one else is home, right?

242
00:16:23,490 --> 00:16:26,320
I will just hand this to you
and leave.

243
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:32,760
- Hey, stop right there.
- Mother, I'm coming in.

244
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:41,810
How dare you set foot in here?

245
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:43,440
Get out right now.

246
00:16:45,010 --> 00:16:46,910
I will leave right after
giving you this, Mother.

247
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:48,150
What is this?

248
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:50,480
The fish-shaped pastries.

249
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:52,850
I asked them
to put in lots of red bean paste.

250
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,520
Did I ask you to buy this for me?

251
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,390
I don't want it,
so take it with you.

252
00:16:58,990 --> 00:17:03,760
I heard you have not been eating.
Please have some while it is warm.

253
00:17:04,430 --> 00:17:05,760
Whether I eat or not,

254
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,630
- what is it to you?
- I'm just worried about you.

255
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:12,170
If you do not eat,
Hak Sung will be upset.

256
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,710
Cut the excuses.

257
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:16,610
I don't know
what scheme you are pulling,

258
00:17:16,670 --> 00:17:19,540
but I won't fall for this.

259
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:22,010
It is nothing like that.

260
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:25,650
Mother, I will take my leave now.

261
00:17:26,450 --> 00:17:27,720
Take good care
of your health, Mother.

262
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,850
And I will leave it here.

263
00:17:29,290 --> 00:17:31,050
Hey, take this with you.

264
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:49,370
How did she know
to buy my favorite thing?

265
00:17:57,010 --> 00:17:58,420
(Fish-Shaped Pastries)

266
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,850
This hits the spot.

267
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:01,950
This is the taste!

268
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:08,730
(Fish-Shaped Pastries)

269
00:18:09,990 --> 00:18:11,360
Maybe it's because
I haven't eaten anything,

270
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:12,830
but it goes down so easily.

271
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:26,580
Mother?

272
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:31,220
Are you eating something over there?

273
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:37,590
What is wrong?

274
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,020
Do you have indigestion?
Can I get you some water?

275
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,860
No, forget the water.

276
00:18:43,630 --> 00:18:46,900
You should have eaten slowly.
This happened because you rushed.

277
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:51,370
I would have to have eaten something
to get indigestion.

278
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:52,940
Are you mocking
your mother-in-law...

279
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,940
who has been starving
in bed all day?

280
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:58,310
No, I just...

281
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,480
Move out of the way.

282
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:05,320
I'm going to lie down in my room.

283
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:09,390
Mother.

284
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:17,690
(Fish-Shaped Pastries)

285
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:27,200
She ate it.

286
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:30,170
At least she ate something.

287
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,150
Oh, no...

288
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:39,420
This is killing me...

289
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,690
Oh, dear...

290
00:19:45,490 --> 00:19:48,160
She cannot find out that I ate it,

291
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:50,930
not after making a big fuss
about not eating.

292
00:19:56,670 --> 00:20:01,140
Oh, dear. My chest hurts.

293
00:20:07,950 --> 00:20:08,950
No.

294
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:13,720
Why does my stomach hurt so much?

295
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:22,090
Oh, dear.

296
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:25,100
My chest hurts.

297
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:29,000
Mi Mi.

298
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:34,710
Mother.

299
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:38,340
- What is wrong?
- I'm dying.

300
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:40,810
I must be dying.

301
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,050
My chest...

302
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,650
It feels so tight.

303
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:46,950
Mother.

304
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:49,750
Just how many of those pastries
did you eat?

305
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,290
Darn it.

306
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,390
She saw everything.

307
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:59,100
What on earth are you talking about?
Were you dreaming?

308
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:02,400
When did I ever eat pastries?

309
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,600
Mother,
let's get to the hospital first.

310
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:08,370
- Can you walk?
- Yes, I can.

311
00:21:09,370 --> 00:21:11,110
Hold onto me like this.

312
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:15,350
- Yes, here.
- My chest hurts.

313
00:21:15,450 --> 00:21:16,850
- It hurts.
- Look here.

314
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:18,750
Look, put on your shoes, Mother.

315
00:21:20,950 --> 00:21:22,050
This way.

316
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:25,020
My chest hurts.

317
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:28,560
Oh my goodness!

318
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:29,660
Where is Director Ju?

319
00:21:29,730 --> 00:21:31,730
Mother suddenly feels tightness
in her chest.

320
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:33,130
Director...

321
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:38,470
What is the matter, Mrs. Choi?
When did you start feeling unwell?

322
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:41,170
Just a little while ago.

323
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:44,110
She has not eaten
since this morning.

324
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:46,840
Then she suddenly ate
a lot of fish-shaped pastries...

325
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:51,180
I told you that's not it.
You were dreaming.

326
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,750
Fish-shaped pastries?

327
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:57,190
Well, let us bring her inside first.
I will examine her first.

328
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,460
- Yes.
- Please come in.

329
00:21:58,460 --> 00:21:59,660
Be careful, Mother.

330
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:03,160
Be careful, take it slow.

331
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:14,170
It seems you are feeling unwell
because you ate too fast.

332
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:18,940
Since you didn't eat earlier,
rest a little while getting an IV.

333
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,610
Let's check your condition.

334
00:22:21,310 --> 00:22:22,810
Why do I need an IV?

335
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:25,650
It is not indigestion;
it is just old age.

336
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,390
- Well...
- I'm just upset, that is all.

337
00:22:29,190 --> 00:22:30,990
That is why
you should get some rest.

338
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:33,090
Since you are here, just get the IV.

339
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:36,190
Lying still makes me feel
even more suffocated.

340
00:22:37,630 --> 00:22:39,730
If you feel uncomfortable,
tell me right away.

341
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,700
I will examine you again.

342
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:45,040
Where should I go?

343
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,170
This way, please.

344
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,110
(Examination Room)

345
00:22:49,170 --> 00:22:50,270
Here.

346
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:57,610
This way.

347
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:00,980
Yes, take your time.

348
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:04,450
(Examination Room)

349
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:12,560
I just need to check on Mrs. Choi
while she gets some rest,

350
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:17,070
but your complexion looks worse.

351
00:23:17,470 --> 00:23:18,600
Are you feeling unwell anywhere?

352
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:22,570
No.
The restaurant has just been busy.

353
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:27,980
Actually, Director Ju.

354
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:31,410
A few days ago,
I got a medical checkup.

355
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,450
My daughter made me do it.

356
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:36,750
I see. Where did you get it done?

357
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:39,260
Haedeul University Hospital.

358
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,290
But they called me today.

359
00:23:42,890 --> 00:23:44,560
They told me to come
hear the results.

360
00:23:45,430 --> 00:23:47,060
They asked if I could come today.

361
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:52,000
Did they mention what it was about?

362
00:23:53,070 --> 00:23:54,340
They said to come in person.

363
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,770
They couldn't explain it
over the phone.

364
00:23:56,740 --> 00:23:59,910
Does that mean it's really bad?

365
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:03,410
You cannot tell
just by looking at a report.

366
00:24:04,150 --> 00:24:05,880
It sounds like they need
to explain it to you,

367
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,680
so you should go in person.

368
00:24:09,550 --> 00:24:12,120
I plan to. I should go.

369
00:24:13,590 --> 00:24:16,060
But Mother is like that,
I have to run the restaurant.

370
00:24:16,330 --> 00:24:18,500
I also have to take care
of Gang Nam and Su Ah.

371
00:24:19,130 --> 00:24:21,160
- Maybe I can put it off today...
- Ms. Jo.

372
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,170
If the hospital told you
to come today,

373
00:24:24,370 --> 00:24:25,540
don't put it off.

374
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:32,110
Still, I have so much to handle,
especially on a day like this.

375
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:36,650
Let me check with the hospital
for you. Just a moment.

376
00:24:36,710 --> 00:24:39,280
You don't have to.
You must be busy too.

377
00:24:42,150 --> 00:24:43,720
It's me, Professor Yoo.

378
00:24:44,790 --> 00:24:46,860
The reason I'm calling is,

379
00:24:47,260 --> 00:24:50,290
someone had a checkup
at your hospital,

380
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:53,160
and she said she got a call
to come in today.

381
00:24:54,700 --> 00:24:56,170
Her name is Jo Mi Mi.

382
00:24:57,530 --> 00:25:00,170
Could you check
when she can be seen today?

383
00:25:02,110 --> 00:25:05,210
Is that right? Okay, got it.

384
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:06,940
All right, thank you.

385
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:16,490
You can head here.

386
00:25:16,850 --> 00:25:18,960
Just give them your name
at reception.

387
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,320
You already set it up?

388
00:25:22,290 --> 00:25:25,030
Yes. Can you go on your own?

389
00:25:25,430 --> 00:25:26,830
Or should I go with you?

390
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:29,470
No, I can go alone.

391
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:32,800
After you did all this for me,
of course I have to go.

392
00:25:34,170 --> 00:25:37,940
Taking care of your family is good,
and the restaurant is important too.

393
00:25:38,410 --> 00:25:39,780
However, I really hope...

394
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:41,850
you take care
of your own health too.

395
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:45,120
Thank you.

396
00:25:45,650 --> 00:25:46,780
I'll be right back.

397
00:25:47,250 --> 00:25:49,590
Yes, please make sure you go.

398
00:25:50,890 --> 00:25:53,520
Then, could you please
take care of my mother-in-law?

399
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:56,890
I will come pick her up
around closing time.

400
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:58,800
Yes.

401
00:26:03,170 --> 00:26:04,170
Bye.

402
00:26:15,180 --> 00:26:16,180
Good.

403
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,190
Seriously...

404
00:26:24,090 --> 00:26:25,620
What is it this time? What happened?

405
00:26:26,390 --> 00:26:29,090
Honey, your mother
came to the hospital.

406
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:31,230
She's in the treatment room
getting an IV right now.

407
00:26:32,130 --> 00:26:33,230
My mom?

408
00:26:34,060 --> 00:26:36,700
- What hurts?
- She said her chest feels tight,

409
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:38,300
and she looks awful.

410
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:41,570
- Is she in bad shape?
- This is our chance.

411
00:26:41,810 --> 00:26:43,010
Get over here right away.

412
00:26:44,910 --> 00:26:48,110
What does she mean, a chance?
She's unbelievable.

413
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:55,350
Why all of a sudden?

414
00:26:57,050 --> 00:26:58,050
Mom.

415
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:04,590
Mom.

416
00:27:04,730 --> 00:27:06,300
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

417
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:10,570
Oh my goodness. Mom.

418
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,170
(Haedeul University Hospital)

419
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:22,650
You are Ms. Jo Mi Mi, correct?

420
00:27:23,310 --> 00:27:26,380
Yes. I came because I got a call.

421
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:30,220
The professor told us
to schedule your tests right away,

422
00:27:30,290 --> 00:27:33,460
so I've been waiting for you.
Please come with me right now.

423
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:37,530
Another test already?

424
00:27:38,900 --> 00:27:39,930
Why?

425
00:27:40,530 --> 00:27:42,530
(Health Screening Center)

426
00:27:56,080 --> 00:27:57,980
(Mission: Mompossible)

427
00:27:58,050 --> 00:28:00,050
About that missing sample box...

428
00:28:00,050 --> 00:28:02,520
I was supposed to take care of
on the new collection review day...

429
00:28:02,690 --> 00:28:06,160
Can you tell me again exactly where
you found that sample box?

430
00:28:06,890 --> 00:28:08,360
Why do an endoscopy again?

431
00:28:08,630 --> 00:28:10,660
Did you put that yellow dress on...

432
00:28:10,790 --> 00:28:14,000
- to go fool around or something?
- Yes, that's right.

433
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:17,570
I lost track of time
dancing with a guy.

434
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:19,100
Happy now?

435
00:28:19,570 --> 00:28:21,570
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
